      {
        "parameters": {
          "promptType": "define",
          "text": "={{ `Analyze the following competitor target:\n- Competitor Name: \"${$json.body.company_name}\"\n- Target Industry: \"${$json.body.industry || 'B2B SaaS'}\"\n\nOperational Instructions:\n1. Verify: First, execute the 'Wikipedia' tool to confirm the competitor's official web domain.\n2. Locate: Find their official pricing page URL (e.g., \"company_name pricing page\") using your general search capability.\n3. Scrape: Call the 'FetchPricingPage' tool, passing the absolute URL of their pricing page as the 'url' parameter.\n4. Extract: Parse the raw text returned by the tool, identify the highest/Enterprise tier, and map the pricing and key features.\n5. Standardize: Formulate your final response to exactly match the structured JSON schema provided.` }}",
          "hasOutputParser": true,
          "needsFallback": true,
          "options": {
            "systemMessage": "Identity: You are an elite B2B Sales Competitive Intelligence Specialist.\nObjective: Your goal is to gather highly accurate and up-to-date information regarding the competitor company provided in the user message.\n\nExecution Loop Instructions:\n1. First, call the 'Wikipedia' tool to verify the official web domain of the competitor.\n2. Once the domain is confirmed, construct a search query to identify their pricing page (e.g., \"company_name pricing page\") and use the 'FetchPricingPage' tool to pull the page's raw data.\n3. Read the retrieved pricing text carefully and isolate the \"Enterprise\" or highest custom tier.\n4. If the pricing page is successfully analyzed, construct your final response strictly matching the required JSON schema.\n\nRules & Constraints:\n- Never make up price values. If an enterprise price is not explicitly listed, return \"Contact Sales\".\n- If any tool execution fails, try a maximum of 2 times before falling back to general knowledge.\n- You must only output the standardized JSON payload. Do not add any conversational preamble or markdown backticks."
          }
        },
        "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
        "typeVersion": 3.1,
        "position": [
          368,
          32
        ],
        "id": "2e564ee9-eefe-4342-8e7b-81b29b6b1e63",
        "name": "CompetitorResearchAgent",
        "retryOnFail": true
      },
